id: pm-vcs-release-gate
title: Release readiness behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED
description: "Prepare daily OIDC publishing behind one repository approval variable. Verify metadata, allowlisted packed files, privacy, regression checks, npm and Bun release gates. The owner performs the first npm publish and trusted-publisher setup; keep approval unset."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:24:17.719Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T03:59:32.974Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:24:26.154Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-25T23:29:54.109Z",codex-agent,"Release simulation inspection found two existing blockers after a calendar version bump: changelog scripts fixed the bootstrap date, and release metadata commits omitted a refreshed self-host archive. Removed the fixed date override while preserving --date-from-version and the existing decide step. The commit step now regenerates and stages selfhost.bundle after staging release metadata. A real temporary Git repository verifies that the committed archive covers the newly staged changelog. Independently restoring either the old workflow step or manifest date makes its regression fail; restored preparation tests pass 2/2."
  "2026-10-26T01:04:02.270Z",codex-agent,"Opening the release-readiness PR after package allowlist/privacy verification and focused regression proofs so complete npm and Bun CI can run in parallel with local full-gate verification. Pending checks are explicitly not treated as passing evidence. No timeout, threshold, dependency pin or test case is being relaxed."
  "2026-10-26T01:37:26.244Z",codex-agent,"Read-only GitHub workflow inspection found release.yml manually disabled. Added a narrowly scoped setup workflow that runs on main when release workflow files change (or on manual main dispatch), verifies the existing approval/provenance/manifest contract, confirms main has not advanced, and only then enables release.yml. It never publishes, configures npm trust or changes a repository variable. This activates the guarded schedule automatically after the owner merges, without enabling the older main workflow now. Missing the setup workflow or removing its main-only guard fails the regression; restored check passes 1/1."
  "2026-10-26T02:25:34.636Z",codex-agent,"Required complete npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASS in isolated GitHub CI at a894f6c03cef736cc52aeedfa4745fc22bc7e433. Main suite counts: npm 1887/1887, Bun 1887/1887; every required matrix job succeeded. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40255206749. The complete gates were verified in isolated CI; they were not duplicated on the already contended local host after that success. Committed-source self-host verification also passed locally. No timeout, case, threshold or dependency pin was changed. Packed artifact allowlist/privacy checks and linked regressions passed. Final tracker evidence is being committed and CI will recheck that final head. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-26T03:35:43.695Z",codex-agent,"PR 152 follow-up: restrict shipped documentation to README-linked guides and examples, scrub machine-specific paths from repository docs, and add a real tarball privacy gate with negative packed-doc regressions. Branch is current with main; no merge needed."
  "2026-10-26T03:41:45.579Z",codex-agent,"Packaging fix: replace broad docs directory inclusion with eleven explicit consumer guides/examples, reducing the packed inventory from 290 to 286 files. Keep certification, audit, receipt and unlinked semantics records in the repository. Neutralized the certification lock path using a TMPDIR placeholder without altering the recorded claim. New pack:check packs with lifecycle scripts disabled, then scans every actual tar member name and contents, including compiled maps, for private paths, hosted-data names and credential shapes; diagnostics omit matched values. Negative real-pack tests cover 19 contamination variants, excluded internal docs, source maps and archive names. Behavioral revert proof: disabling only the classifier makes the packed-guide regression fail (exit 1, missing absolute-home-path finding); restored scanner passes. Initial targeted tests 10/10; new verifier coverage 100/100/100/100; linked pm commands 4/4; typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings and the 286-file package scan pass. Final checks and CI will verify the committed result."
  "2026-10-26T03:59:32.974Z",codex-agent,"First CI run 40265487199 found one failure on each Node version: the explicit production-source inventory still expected 80 files after adding the pack verifier. Updated it to 81 and asserted that the new verifier is included. No coverage threshold or case was removed. The initial complete suites each ran 1893 tests with only that inventory assertion failing; measured coverage remained 100/100/100/100. Pack regressions passed. Rechecking the inventory locally before rerunning both complete npm and Bun CI gates."
